{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate","id":1109829,"title":"Where to Start? Advices for a Neonate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T10:46:29-07:00","id":1109829,"title":"Where to Start? Advices for a Neonate","content":"So. i recently got first edition of requiem, i been curious about the setting for a while (big fan of the Classic World of Darkness). but i would love to know what are the &quot;Must Read&quot; list from Requiem, where should i go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:52:05-07:00","id":1109833,"title":"","content":"Blood sorcery<br /> Danse Macabre<br /> The Clanbooks<br /> <br /> I'd summarize but my keyboard is broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T11:29:56-07:00","id":1109848,"title":"","content":"I'd add Dannation City to that list but the clan books are top of the list as they manage to capture the &quot;this sucks&quot; of being under the thum of someone more powerful but bare in mind everything we've said so far is first ed.<br /> The Chroniclers Guide is also something I find myself rereading quite often and as it's mostly rules free you don't have to worry about it being out of date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:07:44-07:00","id":1109857,"title":"","content":"I'd mostly encourage you to throw 1e out the window and immediately buy 2e instead.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Danse Macabre, Damnation City, and both Night Horrors books are the clear winners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:45:25-07:00","id":1109919,"title":"","content":"I am gonna be the dissenting voice here, this year i have systematically been reading all the Requiem books so this is my recommendation.<br /> <br /> After the Core rulebook i recommend the Covenants ones, NOT Secret of the covenant. The covenants books all expand on the covenants and make them make sense and stand alone as entities. All of the them are full of useful info about how the covenant works. Skip the last 2 chapters they all are an NPC chapter and 1 with the covenant special power which are mostly &quot;obsolete&quot; as 2nd edition has the rules you need for them. Weaker of them all is Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Damnation city:</b></u> It explore on the neofeudal city but i will personally say read chapter 1, 2, 5 and 6. The others are chapters are not that good.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood Sorcery </b></u>is good but only the first chapter. Threnodines are, complicated and even maybe not worth it now in second edition. The idea of the magic of the edgy poetry is cool enough but it actual power in 2nd edition is lukewarm.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Coteries </u></b>is only useful for its first chapter which has info on multicovenant coterie but the rest is better covered on the covenant books.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The blood:</b></u> Marginally useful. First chapter Chargen advice that you dont need if you have been playing for a while, Second chapter is optional rules for 1st edition. And 3rd chapter has fluff on the psychology of vampires which i found very basic. Ravenloft has better advice to be honest.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Danse Macabre: </b></u>First chapter more ST advice on tier of game (Local, regional, global) pretty standard, Second chapter is alternative covenants which is mix bag so its gonna depend if one of them click with you and you wanna change the setting to incorporate them. 3rd chapter optional rules for 1st (Humanity, social combat etc). There is the nice rules for Gargoyles which there isnt a 2nd update yet.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Ghouls: </b></u>Rules for animal ghouls and plant ghouls. The rest is pretty similar to Masquerade material.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Belials Brood:</b></u> Good book but nothing to write home about. It gives you plenty of factions for Belials but nothing too shinny.<br /> <br /> <u><b>VII:</b></u> Its not a good book honestly but VII is not very good by itself. What it gives are possible origins, wildly different for VII. All of them are horrible IMO but maybe you like one of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And this is where i get to the dissenting part. I dont recommend the Clanbooks. They are of limited use at best and glorified fiction at worst. Clans in Requiem are meaningless unless you, as a DM, want to make them a thing. Covenant is where you politic standing is gonna dwell and the Clanbooks are just fluffy stories about NPCs doing stuff in a context with little to no exploring. <br /> <br /> Is my same grip with secret of the Covenant. Is a useless book. Its all feeling and no data on how the covenant manage things or run the day to day business. Reading about character doing stuff in a city which is controlled by a Carthian who forbids the Circle and Lancea is not really useful if i dont know how that city works and how and why it runs the way it does or why thats rare/common. Same with the Clan books, Clan dont have a political structure inherent to them so all i am reading is fiction, that really doesn't help me to run a game because the conditions that put the characters where they are, are unique to them. If you read masquerade books picture a book made entirely of the usual first fiction on the beginning of the book that most people skip. <br /> <br /> For a better example: Reading the Secret of the covenants Lancea Sactum section vs The Lancea Sanctum covenant book. One dweel on a member who had a relationship with a Acolyte of the Circle, they broke up and both have to go to a meeting but the main plot is that the &quot;prince&quot; is acting erratically. The other explains to you the dogma, indoctrination and ranks of the Lancea. The latter is infinitely more useful to run a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T15:44:24-07:00","id":1109950,"title":"","content":"Having not read Secrets of the Covenants I didn't want to recommend the covenant books incase they were out of date. I'm of the opinion that calling The Blood &quot;Marginally useful&quot; is being generous. I do feel the clan books capture the feel of the clans quite well but if that isn't what you're looking for then they can be skipped.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1754_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1754\" data-vbnamecard=\"1754\">Crowley</a> what sort of content are you looking for? If hard rules are your thing then keeping to second edition is good advice but if your looking for fluff then many of our recommendations stand, also what budget are you working on? That may matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:16:39-07:00","id":1109973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1109950#post1109950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having not read Secrets of the Covenants I didn't want to recommend the covenant books incase they were out of date. I'm of the opinion that calling The Blood &quot;Marginally useful&quot; is being generous. I do feel the clan books capture the feel of the clans quite well but if that isn't what you're looking for then they can be skipped.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1754_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1754\" data-vbnamecard=\"1754\">Crowley</a> what sort of content are you looking for? If hard rules are your thing then keeping to second edition is good advice but if your looking for fluff then many of our recommendations stand, also what budget are you working on? That may matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i got enough budget. but mainly im looking to understand more about the Canon of the game, the big events, the evolution of vampires. to become a....Jack of all trades when it comes to its lore mainly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T00:57:33-07:00","id":1110091,"title":"","content":"For canon lore be advised that there isn't much because Requiem tried to move away from anything that could restrict STs from doing their own story but some of the clan books touch on creation myths (only myths, nothing is proven). Requiem of Rome and Fall of the Camarila offer some stuff that may be considered canon but it's not likely to come up in game. Someone who's read One Thosand Years of Night, Night Horrors and Dark Ages will tell you if they have anything you want but I suspect they will. The first edition covenant books cover things like titles and their origin that may come in handy.<br /> I've never played Masquerade but I'm aware of it being criticised for the Meta-Plot getting in the way of individual storys and Requiem seems designed to prevent that from happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:14:32-07:00","id":1110352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110091#post1110091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For canon lore be advised that there isn't much because Requiem tried to move away from anything that could restrict STs from doing their own story but some of the clan books touch on creation myths (only myths, nothing is proven). Requiem of Rome and Fall of the Camarila offer some stuff that may be considered canon but it's not likely to come up in game. Someone who's read One Thosand Years of Night, Night Horrors and Dark Ages will tell you if they have anything you want but I suspect they will. The first edition covenant books cover things like titles and their origin that may come in handy.<br /> I've never played Masquerade but I'm aware of it being criticised for the Meta-Plot getting in the way of individual storys and Requiem seems designed to prevent that from happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one exception is the Real Life mandated meta-plot surrounding New Orleans's kindred, since that source book was published right before katrina hit the city, so they threw in a few updates based on that in the Clanbooks, and in secrets of the covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:22:41-07:00","id":1110354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1109973#post1109973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i got enough budget. but mainly im looking to understand more about the Canon of the game, the big events, the evolution of vampires. to become a....Jack of all trades when it comes to its lore mainly</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats gonna be difficult, there is lot of &quot;choose you own metaplot/setting&quot; parts on the line. However again i will recommend the Covenants books who have the story of each of them. Things like how historically the First State (the invictus) allied himself with the Second State (The lancea) in a mutual alliance of convenience and thats why latter got the name.<br /> <br /> Mythologies has some posibilities on origins for the kindred. The testament of longuinus &amp; The Rites of the Dragons are books that exist in setting and are written IC like the Book of Nod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:27:29-07:00","id":1110359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110354#post1110354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats gonna be difficult, there is lot of &quot;choose you own metaplot/setting&quot; parts on the line. However again i will recommend the Covenants books who have the story of each of them. Things like how historically the First State (the invictus) allied himself with the Second State (The lancea) in a mutual alliance of convenience and thats why latter got the name.<br /> <br /> Mythologies has some posibilities on origins for the kindred. The testament of longuinus &amp; The Rites of the Dragons are books that exist in setting and are written IC like the Book of Nod.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as lore and history goes, The ancient duology and New Wave Requiem are both good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:43:55-07:00","id":1110371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1109973#post1109973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> i got enough budget. but mainly im looking to understand more about the Canon of the game, the big events, the evolution of vampires. to become a....Jack of all trades when it comes to its lore mainly</div> </div> </div> </div>The canon is essentially what you make of it. There are some definite arcs that get detailed in bits and pieces across the fluff of the various books, but you are free to ignore it. And even then, you can ignore established fluff: Secrets of the Covenants establishes that New York is about as close to a functional Carthian domain as you can get, but nothing's stopping you from saying, &quot;In my Chronicle, the Invictus have ruled New York for centuries, and the Carthians only emerged after rebelling against the First Estate in the 60s/70s.&quot; Did the Carthians get started centuries before the books say they did by Italian vampires tired of the Invictus and Sanctified ruling with an iron fist back in the Renaissance? Is London the unofficial Mecca of the Circle of the Crone? It's all up to you to decide. And nothing's going to stop you from making that choice. <br /> <br /> But if you want the Cliffnotes version of how the books present it: <br /> <br /> Nobody knows exactly how the Kindred started in Requiem, but some of the more prominent rumors hold that the Daeva started in Mesopotamia with Inanna and Lilith, the Gangrel evolved out of immortal beast men on the borders of the Roman Empire, the Mekhet were priests of Set who tore out their souls and became undead to fight a Lovecraftian monster summoned by Akhenaten, the Nosferatu were creatures who ate a Lovecraftian creature deep in the earth, and the Ventrue were once the ancestor spirits of Troy. There's also the Julii, who are/were relatives of the Ventrue from Rome, but they got (mostly) wiped out after they went back on a deal with owl-like spirits called the Striges, who destroyed the Julii and Requiem's equivalent of the Camarilla around the time that the Western Roman Empire fell. <br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum was founded by vampires who followed the teachings of Longinus, who claimed he had been Embraced by the blood of Jesus at the Crucifixion and told by God to be a prophet to vampires, teaching them to test the faithful and punish sinners. It suffered a major split in its membership over matters of doctrine and ritual in Elizabethan England. <br /> <br /> The Invictus is the sort-of successor of the Camarilla, but new fluff from SotC suggests that they were originally vampiric members of the Praetorian Guard who allied with the Striges and turned on the Julii, the Camarilla, and Rome itself after the Praetorian Guard was disbanded- or made a new pact with the Striges when it became clear that the Camarilla was failing and the Julii were losing their (tenuous) grip on reality to try and preserve what could be saved. <br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul was founded by Dracula himself as a product of his attempts to understand the vampiric condition and overcome its limitations. <br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement was supposedly founded in France during the time of the Revolution as a rebellion against the tyranny of elders over neonates- though SotC suggests that the Movement may have started in New York. <br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone is a loose federation of differing vampiric faiths who banded together to rally against oppression by the Lancea et Sanctum and to preserve their way of life. <br /> <br /> VII is a mysterious assortment of vampires who hunt other vampires, leaving only a symbol resembling the Roman numeral VII at the scene of the murders. They may have been founded by a &quot;lost&quot; clan called the Akhud, who originated in Sodom and Gomorrah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T06:01:33-07:00","id":1110524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110359#post1110359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ancient duology.</div> </div> </div> </div>The what now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T07:12:17-07:00","id":1110534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110524#post1110524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The what now?</div> </div> </div> </div>The books Ancient Mysteries and Ancient Bloodlines.<br /> Mysteries talks about playing elder characters (only not as in depth and, imo, not as well as Thousand Years of Night) as well as describing ten different eras around the world (with one example character per era).<br /> Bloodlines expand somewhat on the same eras by introducing two bloodlines per era plus something extra per era.<br /> <br /> They're good for getting some Kindred history. I personally love Black Streets of Babylon and Ancient Egypt (the only two eras that I consider actually ancient despite the names of the two books). Only problem is that the history probably won't show up much in modern nights, and the eras I've read aren't written in ways that allow you to use them as settings. Thousand Years of Night does the whole elder thing a lot better, and the few vampire specific entries in Dark Eras (+Companion) is much better at describing playable eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T02:39:18-07:00","id":1110791,"title":"","content":"For historical events: Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla, Ancient Mysteries, Covenanr books and Ventrue clanbook (it has a detailed section about Ventrue history), Requiem gor Regina (Dark Eras) and theBlack Death chapter from Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:32:43-07:00","id":1110818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1109857#post1109857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd mostly encourage you to throw 1e out the window and immediately buy 2e instead.<br /> <br /> Other than that, Danse Macabre, Damnation City, and both Night Horrors books are the clear winners.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only 2ed would expand on Bloodlines and maybe bring back Derangements...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:59:55-07:00","id":1110828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110818#post1110818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If only 2ed would expand on Bloodlines and maybe bring back Derangements...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for derangements you have conditions, which quite a few can be persistent, like broken or addiction. Then we have the Morbus, Neglatu, Khaibit, and a fourth bloodline that have been updated to second edition, and a basic explanation of bloodlines in the core book. I'm actually not sure why there wasn't much mention of bloodlines in 1000 years of night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:39:11-07:00","id":1110844,"title":"","content":"I would also toss my suggestion behind going to 2e. Personally love the slight but significant change in general feel of the vampires.<br /> <br /> Though the supplement 1e books suggested by others are still very good to pick up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T08:04:41-07:00","id":1110857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110828#post1110828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for derangements you have conditions, which quite a few can be persistent, like broken or addiction. Then we have the Morbus, Neglatu, Khaibit, and a fourth bloodline that have been updated to second edition, and a basic explanation of bloodlines in the core book. I'm actually not sure why there wasn't much mention of bloodlines in 1000 years of night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess conditions can be homebrewed to represent some derangements.<br /> <br /> And Morbus was officially converted? Where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:12:14-07:00","id":1110875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110857#post1110857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess conditions can be homebrewed to represent some derangements.<br /> <br /> And Morbus was officially converted? Where?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conditions <i>are</i> the second edition's verison of derangements (among other things). At least for those derangements that weren't horribly inappropriate and appropriately excised. The books just don't tell you that you can take a persistent Condition at character creation.<br /> <br /> Morbus' in Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:42:01-07:00","id":1110893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110875#post1110875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conditions <i>are</i> the second edition's verison of derangements (among other things). At least for those derangements that weren't horribly inappropriate and appropriately excised. The books just don't tell you that you can take a persistent Condition at character creation.<br /> <br /> Morbus' in Dark Eras Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess the only proper way to portray mental illness is by roleplaying it than using it as a mechanic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:50:45-07:00","id":1110919,"title":"","content":"If you're playing 1st edition, I'd recommend the Carthian and Invictus books. The core book only gives them cost breaks, they didn't get &quot;powers&quot; (Carthian Law and Invictus Oaths) until the covenant books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:57:58-07:00","id":1110993,"title":"","content":"I've never heard of Bloodlines : the forgotten, is there perhaps an English version? And for my own suggestions, The LA Fanbook isn't bad, and the clan books do tend to give you a better view on the clans from their own perspective, than any other first edition book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12527-thearcane","name":"TheArcane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12527_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:37:12-07:00","id":1111215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110371#post1110371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;In my Chronicle, the Invictus have ruled New York for centuries&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well before Secrets of the Covenants came out the New York I made was a 100% Invictus Domain, I took the whole &quot;Empire City&quot; thing too far and even the Prince styled himself as the Emperor of New York.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:13:49-07:00","id":1111291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1111215#post1111215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well before Secrets of the Covenants came out the New York I made was a 100% Invictus Domain, I took the whole &quot;Empire City&quot; thing too far and even the Prince styled himself as the Emperor of New York.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked up the Joe Pitt Casebooks as a recommendation from the 2e corebook, and the set-up of the &quot;Clans&quot; is pretty rich fuel for an &quot;alternate&quot; take on the city: the Invictus runs the city; the Carthians formed out of a rebellion in the 60s and 70s, but the rebels split into two factions, one made up of political progressives and sexual minorities, and the others based in Harlem made up of African-Americans and Latinos; the Ordo Dracul, whom everybody ignores for their own good, because those guys are <i>crazy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T21:58:10-07:00","id":1111554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheArcane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1109829-where-to-start-advices-for-a-neonate?p=1110993#post1110993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never heard of Bloodlines : the forgotten, is there perhaps an English version? And for my own suggestions, The LA Fanbook isn't bad, and the clan books do tend to give you a better view on the clans from their own perspective, than any other first edition book.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Bloodlines: The forgotten. There's no English version (but feel free to translate if you want). It was a fanbook from submissions of fans to our website (Requiem Nocte). There's some bloodlines, IMO, really good, but others I would burn them.<br /> <br /> From my own fanbooks, I prefer both books about Spain (although they're first edition). Both are very strong in the history aspects and the first one introducrs new bloodlines and ghoul families.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 07-05-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T12:33:17-07:00","id":1120444,"title":"","content":"Also, kind of a funny question. i been looking for the second edition books on amazon andebay...buuut....the cover on the second edition is identical to the first ed so...anyone got a link (hopefully not that expensive) to get some of the second ed books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T12:36:59-07:00","id":1120446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a